`aws:SourceIp`

Example:
```json
"Condition": {
  "IpAddress": {
    "aws:SourceIp": "203.0.113.0/24"
  }
}
```

Note: For VPC endpoint requests, use `aws:SourceVpc` or `aws:SourceVpce` instead.

A **bucket policy** with a `Deny` condition on `s3:PutObject` when `s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption` is absent or not set to an approved value.

Example condition:
```json
"Condition": {
  "StringNotEquals": {
    "s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption": "AES256"
  }
}
```

Alternatively, enable **Default Encryption** on the bucket (SSE-S3 or SSE-KMS) to auto-encrypt objects on upload.

It enforces **HTTPS-only access** to the bucket.

Set a `Deny` on all actions when `aws:SecureTransport` is `false`:
```json
"Condition": {
  "Bool": { "aws:SecureTransport": "false" }
}
```
This blocks any request made over HTTP (plaintext), ensuring data in transit is encrypted.
